# Options for smartd (storage housekeeping, P-10). Debian's smartmontools.service reads smartd_opts from here.
# -q nodev0  a box with no disk that speaks SMART (every virtual machine, some USB bridges) starts smartd and exits
#            cleanly instead of failing, so the Services screen and the Storage card do not show "failed".
# --interval=1800  look at the disks every 30 minutes (Debian's default).
smartd_opts="--interval=1800 -q nodev0"
